From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:58:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 033/220] [ae-patch] File each scheduled task run into the
 task's project

Every firing of a scheduled task opens a new session outside any project, so
automation runs pile up unfiled in the sidebar. Reid decided on 2026-10-13
that a task names a project its runs open in, with a server-configured
default for new tasks (Automation Notes on the AE box).

- omnigent/server/scheduled/task_project.py (new): project_id stored in its
  own table, ae_scheduled_task_project, created on first use, so no Alembic
  revision is needed; the default project named by
  OMNIGENT_SCHEDULED_TASK_DEFAULT_PROJECT, resolved per owner by name and
  stored by id; and file_fired_session, which files the new session with
  set_conversation_project after checking the owner still has the project.
  A missing project or store error leaves the run unfiled and never fails
  the fire.
- project_id on ScheduledTask and on /v1/scheduled-tasks create, patch, get
  and list. It must name one of the caller's projects (404 otherwise); null
  or "" leaves runs unfiled; a create that omits it gets the default. Plus
  the sys_scheduled_task_create/update tool schemas and dispatch allowlists.
- fire.py gains an import, a FireDeps field and one call after the session
  is created; app.py passes project_store to the router and FireDeps.
- web: a Project picker on the automation dialog (AeTaskProjectField, new);
  "Default project" on create omits the field so the server default applies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
